    "sl_custom_faq_r7Q6ht": {
      "type": "sl-custom-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_qjMHfp": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How painful is Brazilian waxing really?",
            "answer": "<p>While everyone's pain tolerance is different, most clients say it's not nearly as bad as they expected! The first time is usually the most uncomfortable, but it gets easier with each visit as your hair becomes finer. Our gentle technique and premium hard wax minimize discomfort, and the whole process takes just 15-20 minutes. The smooth results for 4-6 weeks are absolutely worth those few minutes!</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_PzXEKn": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does my hair need to be?",
            "answer": "<p>Your hair should be about 1/4 inch long (about the length of a grain of rice) for best results. This typically means waiting 2-3 weeks after shaving or 4-6 weeks after your last wax. If it's longer, that's okay too - we can trim if needed. Avoid the temptation to shave between appointments as this disrupts the hair growth cycle!</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_GmWhMf": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if I'm on my period?",
            "answer": "<p>You can absolutely get waxed during your period! Just wear a fresh tampon or cup to your appointment. Keep in mind you may be slightly more sensitive during this time, but many clients don't notice a difference. We're professionals and want you to feel comfortable maintaining your waxing schedule.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_PGh67J": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I prevent ingrown hairs?",
            "answer": "<p>Prevention is key! Start gently exfoliating 48 hours after your wax, 2-3 times per week. Keep the area moisturized daily, wear loose cotton underwear when possible, and avoid tight clothing immediately after waxing. We'll provide you with specific aftercare instructions and recommend products that actually work. Most clients see a dramatic reduction in ingrowns when they follow our routine.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_XkqtLR": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is Brazilian waxing worth the cost?",
            "answer": "<p>Absolutely! When you calculate the time and money spent on razors, shaving cream, and dealing with razor burn and ingrowns, professional waxing is actually cost-effective. Plus, you can't put a price on the confidence of being smooth for weeks, the reduction in hair growth over time, and healthier skin overall. Most clients say they wish they'd started sooner!</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_P6KPXe": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What should I do to prepare for my appointment?",
            "answer": "<p>Gently exfoliate the day before, avoid caffeine the day of (it can increase sensitivity), and wear comfortable, loose clothing to your appointment. Don't apply any lotions or oils the day of your service. Take an ibuprofen 30 minutes before if you're concerned about discomfort. Most importantly, relax - we'll take great care of you!</p>"
          }
        }
      },
